    "text": {
     "en": "India is home to many religions, including Hinduism, Islam, Christianity, Sikhism, Buddhism and Jainism. People of different religions live as neighbours.\nThe Constitution recognises 22 languages in the Eighth Schedule, and hundreds of dialects are spoken.\nEach state has a language, a cuisine and a dress, and festivals show the variety."
    }
